WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.125
Week 28: Subjunctive: Doubt, Purpose, and Contingency. qualify certainty state purpose and conditions plan for contingencies

2
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:22.263
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can qualify certainty, state purpose and conditions, plan for contingencies. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:22.263 --> 00:00:31.942
Language system. Subjunctive with doubt/denial; adverbial clauses; antes de que, para que, a menos que, and cuando with future reference.

4
00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:38.059
Sound and delivery. Clause grouping and contrastive emphasis on certainty markers.

5
00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:47.485
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:47.485 --> 00:01:15.236
Model language. Dudo que la cifra sea correcta. — I doubt that the figure is correct. Es probable que llueva esta noche. — It will probably rain tonight. Salimos temprano para que haya tiempo suficiente. — We are leaving early so that there is enough time. No firmaremos a menos que cambien la cláusula. — We will not sign unless they change the clause. Llámame en cuanto llegues. — Call me as soon as you arrive.

7
00:01:15.236 --> 00:01:25.155
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
